UPDATE courses SET
    course_description = '<p style="text-align: justify;">This qualification reflects the role of experienced building professionals who apply their knowledge of structural principles, risk and financial management, estimating, contract administration, contractor selection, quality control, and site management to residential and commercial building projects. Residential construction is limited to National Construction Code (NCC) Class 1 and 10 buildings, up to a maximum of three storeys. Commercial construction is limited to NCC Class 2 to 9 buildings, Type B and Type C constructions. Occupational titles may include Builder, General Foreperson, and Building Inspector. The construction industry strongly supports that training and assessment must take place in a real or closely simulated workplace environment to ensure the authenticity and relevance of skills developed.</p> <p style="text-align: justify;">Occupational titles may include: <ul> <li>Residential construction limited to National Construction Code Class 1 and 10 buildings to a maximum of 3 storeys. </li> <li>Commercial construction limited to National Construction Code Class 2 to 9 buildings, Type C and B construction. Occupational titles may include: </li> <li>Builder · General Foreperson · Building Inspector.</li> </ul> </p> <li>Residential construction limited to National Construction Code Class 1 and 10 buildings to a maximum of 3 storeys. </li> <li>Commercial construction limited to National Construction Code Class 2 to 9 buildings, Type C and B construction. Occupational titles may include: </li> <li>Builder · General Foreperson · Building Inspector.</li> <p style="text-align: justify;">The construction industry strongly affirms that training and assessment leading to recognition of skills must be undertaken in a real or very closely simulated workplace environment. To achieve this qualification, the candidate must have access to a live building and construction workplace to meet the requirements detailed in the Assessment Requirements of core unit CPCCBC4008 Supervise communication and administration processes for building and construction projects.</p> <p style="text-align: justify;">Completion of the general construction induction training program specified by the model Code of Practice for Construction Work is required for any person who is to carry out construction work. Achievement of unit CPCCWHS1001 Prepare to work safely in the construction industry meets this requirement. Builder licensing varies across States and Territories and requirements additional to the attainment of this qualification may be required.</p>',
    total_course_duration = '78 Weeks',
    offshore_tuition_fee = '',
    entry_requirements = '<p>The following are the Admission requirements of Lead college:</p> <li>Must be 18 years of age or older at the time of course commencement.</li> <li>Prospective students may be required to undertake a Language, Literacy and Numeracy (LLN) and/or a pre-enrolment interview.</li> <li>Must have completed Australian Year 12 or equivalent level of schooling or a Certificate III or higher qualification with an Australian institution.</li> <li>Must demonstrate English level of IELTS 6.0 overall with no band less than 5.5 or equivalent, such as: <ul> <li>IBT 60 <li>PTE 50 <li>CAE 169 <li>OET B <li>General English Advanced or equivalent <li>MOI Certificate <li>Duolingo 95 <li>MET <li>LANGUAGECERT Academic <li>CELPIP General <li>Certificate IV or higher qualification with an Australian institution.</li> </li></li></li></li></li></li></li></li></li></li></ul> </li> <li>IBT 60 <li>PTE 50 <li>CAE 169 <li>OET B <li>General English Advanced or equivalent <li>MOI Certificate <li>Duolingo 95 <li>MET <li>LANGUAGECERT Academic <li>CELPIP General <li>Certificate IV or higher qualification with an Australian institution.</li> </li></li></li></li></li></li></li></li></li></li> <li>PTE 50 <li>CAE 169 <li>OET B <li>General English Advanced or equivalent <li>MOI Certificate <li>Duolingo 95 <li>MET <li>LANGUAGECERT Academic <li>CELPIP General <li>Certificate IV or higher qualification with an Australian institution.</li> </li></li></li></li></li></li></li></li></li> <li>CAE 169 <li>OET B <li>General English Advanced or equivalent <li>MOI Certificate <li>Duolingo 95 <li>MET <li>LANGUAGECERT Academic <li>CELPIP General <li>Certificate IV or higher qualification with an Australian institution.</li> </li></li></li></li></li></li></li></li> <li>OET B <li>General English Advanced or equivalent <li>MOI Certificate <li>Duolingo 95 <li>MET <li>LANGUAGECERT Academic <li>CELPIP General <li>Certificate IV or higher qualification with an Australian institution.</li> </li></li></li></li></li></li></li> <li>General English Advanced or equivalent <li>MOI Certificate <li>Duolingo 95 <li>MET <li>LANGUAGECERT Academic <li>CELPIP General <li>Certificate IV or higher qualification with an Australian institution.</li> </li></li></li></li></li></li> <li>MOI Certificate <li>Duolingo 95 <li>MET <li>LANGUAGECERT Academic <li>CELPIP General <li>Certificate IV or higher qualification with an Australian institution.</li> </li></li></li></li></li> <li>Duolingo 95 <li>MET <li>LANGUAGECERT Academic <li>CELPIP General <li>Certificate IV or higher qualification with an Australian institution.</li> </li></li></li></li> <li>MET <li>LANGUAGECERT Academic <li>CELPIP General <li>Certificate IV or higher qualification with an Australian institution.</li> </li></li></li> <li>LANGUAGECERT Academic <li>CELPIP General <li>Certificate IV or higher qualification with an Australian institution.</li> </li></li> <li>CELPIP General <li>Certificate IV or higher qualification with an Australian institution.</li> </li> <li>Certificate IV or higher qualification with an Australian institution.</li> <li>Must have basic digital literacy, including the ability to confidently use the internet and common software applications for learning purposes, completing assignments, and engaging with course content.</li> <li>Must be able to participate in training within a simulated workplace environment, including performing manual handling tasks.</li>',
